            <div xml:id="d127">

                <pb facs="0143" n="131" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg131"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.6215/26: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-02-17T15:00:00+03:00">February 17,
                            1941—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 17—2:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>295. My 51, January 11. <hi rendition="#italic">Pravda</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Izvestiya</hi> of February 16 report the arrival in
                    Moscow on February 15 of a German delegation to the Central Joint Soviet-German
                    Frontier Commission for the demarcation of the Soviet-German frontier from the
                    River Igorka to the Baltic Sea. The delegation which is reported as consisting
                    of six members was met at the station by members of the Soviet delegation to the
                    Commission mentioned and by officials of the German Embassy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
